From: Guanyi Chen <felixlinker02@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] amdgpu: bypass P2P distance check in dma_buf_attach

pci_p2pdma_distance() can return a negative value on certain PCIe
topologies (GPU and NVMe across root complex), which disables the
peer2peer flag and prevents VRAM P2P DMA entirely.

Bypass the check so that P2P is always allowed. On platforms where the
distance is already positive (e.g., MI210 returns 6), this is a no-op.

Signed-off-by: Guanyi Chen <felixlinker02@gmail.com>
---
 amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_dma_buf.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_dma_buf.c b/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_dma_buf.c
index abcdef1..1234567 100644
--- a/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_dma_buf.c
+++ b/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_dma_buf.c
@@ -236,7 +236,7 @@
 	struct amdgpu_device *adev = amdgpu_ttm_adev(bo->tbo.bdev);
 
 #ifdef HAVE_STRUCT_DMA_BUF_ATTACH_OPS_ALLOW_PEER2PEER
-	if (pci_p2pdma_distance(adev->pdev, attach->dev, true) < 0)
+	if (0)
 		attach->peer2peer = false;
 #endif
 
